using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace K2.Core;

/// <summary>
/// Real vector logos (Simple Icons / MDI, single-path 0-0-24-24 glyphs, CC0/Apache-licensed)
/// for the picker cards that represent an actual app/service or a well-known concept, instead
/// of a generic emoji — used by ButtonActionDialog.TypePicker.cs wherever a tag has one.
/// Path data pulled from https://api.iconify.design (simple-icons/mdi collections) 2026-08-24.
/// Colors are each brand's official hex where it reads on the dialog's dark card background;
/// a few official colors are near-black (OBS/DaVinci/Windows Terminal) and get a neutral
/// light-gray substitute instead so the icon stays visible.
/// </summary>
internal static class ButtonActionDialogIcons
{
    /// <summary><paramref name="Width"/>/<paramref name="Height"/> are the on-card display
    /// box in DIPs — square for the usual 24x24 logo, but a wordmark (Zoom) needs a box
    /// matching its own aspect ratio or Stretch=Uniform would shrink it to a sliver.</summary>
    internal readonly record struct VectorIcon(string PathData, string Color, double Width = 20, double Height = 20);

    /// <summary>Multi-color logos that can't be a single-path vector, shipped as small
    /// cropped PNGs instead (see K2.Core.csproj) — the two the user supplied directly.</summary>
    internal readonly record struct ImageIcon(string PackUri, double Width = 22, double Height = 22);

